{"term":"Scopophilie","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"voyeurism","concept":"voyeurism","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":10,"technical":90,"recognition_pct_current":18,"recognition_pct_peak":18,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The German clinical term for scopophilia; a paraphilia characterized by sexual arousal derived from watching the intimate behavior, nudity, or sexual activity of others, typically without their knowledge.","english_term":"scopophilia","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"In German clinical sexology essentially synonymous with Voyeurismus; 'Scopophilie' appears in older psychiatric literature and is rarer in contemporary usage than Voyeurismus; derived from Greek skopein (to look)."}
{"term":"BDSM","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"bdsm","concept":"bdsm","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":40,"technical":30,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The same acronym used in German as in English, expanding as Bondage/Disziplin, Dominanz/Submission, Sadismus/Masochismus; the umbrella term for consensual power-exchange and pain-play sexual practices and the community around them.","english_term":"BDSM","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Identical acronym and meaning across languages; fully absorbed into German BDSM community vocabulary and mainstream awareness via media; the German expansion maps cleanly onto the English one."}
{"term":"Bondage","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"bondage","concept":"bondage","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"loanword","crude":45,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Direct English loanword used unchanged in German BDSM contexts for the practice of physically restraining a partner with rope, cuffs, or other materials for sexual arousal or power exchange.","english_term":"bondage","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The German BDSM community uses the English term rather than native equivalents such as 'Fesselung'; mainstream recognition has grown substantially through media exposure of BDSM themes."}
{"term":"Dominanz","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"dominance","concept":"sexual_dominance","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":25,"technical":45,"recognition_pct_current":93,"recognition_pct_peak":93,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"German word for 'dominance'; in BDSM contexts refers specifically to the role of holding authority and control over a submissive partner within a consensual power-exchange dynamic.","english_term":"dominance","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Dominanz' is a standard German noun with broad non-sexual uses (social dominance, biological dominance, chess); its BDSM-specific meaning is one register among several and widely understood in context."}
