{"term":"Dominatrix","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"female_dominant","concept":"bdsm_dominant_female","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"loanword","crude":55,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"English/Latin loanword in German for a woman who takes the dominant role in BDSM activity, often specifically implying a professional who offers paid dominance sessions.","english_term":"dominatrix","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Used alongside the more community-native 'Domina'; 'Dominatrix' tends to appear in mainstream media and journalistic contexts while 'Domina' is preferred within the professional and community sphere."}
{"term":"Domina","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"female_dominant","concept":"bdsm_dominant_female","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":50,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":84,"recognition_pct_peak":84,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"German/Latin term for a female dominant in BDSM; the standard community and professional term in German-speaking countries for a woman who exercises dominance over submissive partners, frequently in a dedicated studio setting.","english_term":"dominatrix","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Derived from Latin 'domina' (lady, mistress, owner); in German-speaking BDSM and professional sex-work contexts 'Domina' is the default label in classified ads, studio names, and community profiles, making it more embedded than 'Dominatrix' in everyday BDSM language."}
{"term":"Herr","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"male_dominant_title","concept":"bdsm_dominant","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":10,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The standard German honorific for 'Mr./Sir/Lord'; in BDSM contexts used as a title of address for a male dominant, functionally equivalent to the English BDSM titles 'Sir' or 'Master.'","english_term":"Sir / Master","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The everyday honorific is universally known; its BDSM usage as a dominant title is a community convention recognized by perhaps 25–35% of adults. Recognition figures reflect the common word, not the BDSM-specific sense."}
{"term":"Herrin","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"female_dominant_title","concept":"bdsm_dominant_female","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":10,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":94,"recognition_pct_peak":94,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The feminine form of 'Herr' meaning 'mistress, lady, owner'; in BDSM contexts used as a title of address for a female dominant, functionally equivalent to the English BDSM title 'Mistress.'","english_term":"Mistress","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Herrin' in its sense of owner or ruler is established in literary and formal German; its BDSM title usage mirrors English 'Mistress.' Recognition of the word is high; BDSM-specific recognition is approximately 25–40% of adults."}
{"term":"Sklave","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"male_submissive","concept":"bdsm_submissive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":35,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"German word for 'slave' (male); in BDSM contexts denotes a male submissive who identifies with a total power exchange or slave dynamic, voluntarily surrendering comprehensive autonomy to a dominant.","english_term":"slave (male)","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The ordinary German word for slave is repurposed as a BDSM identity label; 'Sklave' implies a deeper, more comprehensive submission than 'Sub,' mirroring the English distinction between slave and submissive within community discourse."}
{"term":"Sklavin","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"kink_paraphilia","subcategory":"female_submissive","concept":"bdsm_submissive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"subculture","crude":35,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"German word for 'slave' (female); in BDSM contexts denotes a female submissive who identifies with a total power exchange or slave dynamic.","english_term":"slave (female)","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Feminine form of 'Sklave'; German grammatical gender makes the male/female distinction obligatory in a way English 'slave' does not; the gendered form is used in community profiles, fiction, and negotiation contexts."}
